==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Waitress Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Soba Cat''' after beating [[Revenge of the Unholy (Merciless)|Revenge of the Unholy]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
When used correctly, Cheerleader Cat can be an amazing asset to your team if you find yourself stuck on a difficult [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] stage where she can deliver lethal critical hits to strong metals and tear them down quickly, crippling if not immediately killing the likes of [[Sir Metal Seal]] and [[Super Metal Hippoe]].

This great strength comes with a great price however, as she takes four seconds to attack and has a 16-second delay between attacks, effectively providing only one critical hit every 20 seconds, which can be detrimental when the frontline shifts or if she hits a weak metal like Metal Doge. Her cooldown doesn't help, either, as it would be slightly over half a minute before you could send another. Notably, her range isn't too high, only 350. This means she will be at a point of risk even with meatshielding, and provided she only has 3 knockbacks, it is important to protect her well if you want to use her effectively.

Never use Cheerleader Cat for her [[Zombie Killer]] ability, as her long attack rate and attack animation often makes her miss burrowing enemies, making her in general unsuitable for countering them. Even if she outranges most Zombie enemies, it is highly recommended to keep her away from the undead.

==='''True Form'''===
In [[True Form]], Soba Cat gains a 25% attack and defense boost. This is almost the same thing as adding an extra 10 levels to Waitress, meaning a level 50 Waitress is almost the equivalent of a level 40 Soba Cat, so it sometimes takes fewer hits for her to kill dangerous enemies by herself, but nothing more. This matters the most if she needs to perform yet another critical hit without the extra damage, forcing you to maintain your defense for a lengthy period. This is especially crucial against [[Super Metal Hippoe]] and [[Sir Metal Seal]], who are two notably bulky metal enemies. In fact, at level 44, Soba Cat can one-shot a 300% Super Metal Hippoe, which would be the most common magnifications starting from [[Legend Stages|Uncanny Legends]]. Overall, the true form is a very much-needed boost for notorious Metal stages, such as [[March to Death (Merciless)]].

In the gallery, there is a graph that explains exactly how much is improved.

