==Trivia==
*Cheerleader Cat was added as a placeholder in [[Version 5.2 Update|Version 5.2]], but went unused until Version 5.6.
*In the foreswing of all her forms, Cheerleader Cat spells out "LOVE" with her arms and body.
*Soba Cat's Japanese name, "にゃんこそば" (''Nyanko Soba''), may be derived from "わんこそば" (''[[wikipedia:Wanko soba|wanko soba]]'') in which small portions of soba noodles are served in repetition. This is supported by the contrast of the replaced words in the context of the game ("わんこ" is [[Doge]]'s Japanese name, and "にゃんこ" represents the Cats) as well as the large number of bowls that Soba Cat carries.

